
  XOS install medium

  The installer starts by itself in a moment. Nothing is erased until you
  have seen the disk and typed its name back.

  If you leave it, or it finishes, you get a shell. From there:

      install-xos               start it again
      install-xos --dry-run     every question, nothing written
      xos hardware              what is in this machine, and what it needs
      iwctl                     connect to wifi
      ip a                      check the network

  There is a full manual at /root/xos/docs/manual.md, and one for running
  XOS with no desktop at /root/xos/docs/headless.md.

